# THE SEPARATION WITNESSES: one pair of points per pair of settings.
#
# A POINT IS AN EXPORTED UNARY PREDICATE of the module that includes this
# file, and a piece defined elsewhere is pulled in by a plain call, which
# yields a fresh copy of that clause's variables; the prelude's pieces reach
# this file through the module's `use_module` of it.
#
# Two settings separate what these points read.
#
# Untabled `weak_head` against `tabling(weak_head)`: `omega` diverges under
# plain weak head reduction, and is decided to have no answer in finite
# time once the reduction is tabled, because its reduct is itself and the
# tabled call re-enters its own variant.
#
# `speculative(Budget, Exhausted, Nesting)` against plain `weak_head`, both
# tabled, witnessed by `growing_argument` below. The speculation runs on
# the argument of each beta reduction before it is substituted; what this
# term needs is that its growing argument be normalised rather than
# substituted as it stands.

λ export. export λ. (λx_0. x_0 x_0) λx_0. x_0 x_0
